    {
      "id": "r20261103-a02",
      "title": "Why Cities Are Building Sponge Parks",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "Heavy rain is causing floods in more and more cities. Concrete and asphalt cannot absorb water, so it flows into the streets. To solve this problem, some cities are building 'sponge parks'.",
        "A sponge park looks like a normal park, but it is designed to hold rainwater. The ground is lower than the streets around it, and it is full of plants and soil that drink up the water like a sponge. During heavy rain, the park fills with water instead of the streets. A few days later, the water slowly sinks into the ground.",
        "These parks do more than stop floods. They give people green space to relax, they keep the city cooler, and they help birds and insects survive in the city. Cities from China to the Netherlands are now building them. Sometimes the best technology is simply a garden."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "floods": "banjir",
        "absorb": "menyerap",
        "designed": "dirancang",
        "soil": "tanah",
        "fills with": "terisi",
        "sinks": "meresap",
        "survive": "bertahan hidup"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "Why do cities flood easily?",
          "opts": [
            "Concrete and asphalt cannot absorb water",
            "It rains every day",
            "The rivers are too small"
          ],
          "a": 0
        },
        {
